      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Neisseria gonorrhoeae moves in pairs, two coffee-bean shaped cells that
    cling together as they cross the battlefield. It slips inside the host's own
    white blood cells and settles in the mucous membranes, spreading quietly from
    one host to the next. Resistance grows with every season, so only a swift, well-aimed
    strike can stop it before it spreads. Treat it early, and the pair never makes
    it past the first lane.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 3914de223fa8efc4787902589e5d6968, type: 2}
