  m_text: Chlamydia trachomatis is a quiet infiltrator that cannot live outside a
    host cell, so it hides inside the very cells it attacks. Often it causes no symptoms
    at all, spreading unseen until it leaves damage behind. Because it lives inside
    cells, only antibiotics that can follow it in can reach it. Once found, the right
    drug clears it completely.
