      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Helicobacter pylori twists across the battlefield like a living corkscrew,
    driving itself forward with a bundle of flagella. It survives the harsh acid
    of the stomach by producing urease, neutralizing the world around it. Left alone,
    it carves ulcers into the stomach wall and quietly raises the risk of cancer.
    Defeating it takes teamwork: more than one antibiotic must strike together.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
