  m_text: Acinetobacter baumannii (CRAB) is the armored heavyweight of the infection
    ward, a hospital survivor that can live for weeks on dry surfaces. It has learned
    to resist even carbapenems, the strongest antibiotics most defenders can offer.
    Ventilators, wounds and medical devices are its hunting ground. When every normal
    weapon fails, only an old last-resort drug is left to face it.
