--- !u!114 &3270245535814282047
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6593573816801309031}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ae993d25d2516f44d9227eea8441a88d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  slotName: {fileID: 2399499057402378444}
  slotDescription: {fileID: 646478692576589320}
  Amoxicillin:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 4825175052472912862}
    button: {fileID: 1557170415752199195}
    name: Amoxicillin
    description: "Amoxicillin is a steadfast guardian on the battlefield, standing
      firm against waves of invading bacteria. Forged from the principles of classic
      antibiotics, it works by weakening bacterial defenses from within, preventing
      them from growing and overwhelming the frontline. Though it does not strike
      with explosive force, Amoxicillin excels at protection and control, slowing
      the enemy\u2019s advance and giving other defenders the time they need to fight
      back. In prolonged battles, its presence can mean the difference between a
      breached line and a fortified defense."
  Vancomisin:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 4390215618978615159}
    button: {fileID: 5684297828193318589}
    name: Vancomisin
    description: "Vancomisin is a last-line defender, deployed only when the battlefield
      faces the most resilient bacterial threats. Unlike common guardians, it strikes
      directly at the enemy\u2019s structural core, tearing apart their defenses
      and halting even the toughest bacteria in their tracks. Slow to deploy but
      devastatingly effective, Vancomycin excels at stopping powerful invasions that
      lesser treatments cannot contain. When the frontline is close to collapse,
      its presence becomes a symbol of resolve unyielding, precise, and relentless
      in protecting the final defense."
  Cefixime:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 2284800590713061893}
    button: {fileID: 7138047470079239564}
    name: Cefixime
    description: Cefixime is a versatile defender designed to maintain control when
      bacterial attacks become unpredictable. It disrupts bacterial growth with steady
      precision, making it especially effective against enemies that slip past basic
      defenses. Not as heavy as last-line guardians, yet more refined than early
      treatments, Cefixime excels at stabilizing the battlefield and preventing sudden
      breakthroughs. In extended engagements, its balanced strength and reliability
      allow the defense line to adapt and endure against evolving bacterial waves.
  Azitromisin:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 4517715180588389397}
    button: {fileID: 1125363196756426394}
    name: Azitromisin
    description: Azitromisin is a swift and adaptive defender, excelling at controlling
      bacterial forces before they can fully overwhelm the field. Rather than relying
      on brute force, it disrupts enemy coordination, slowing their advance and weakening
      their ability to multiply. Its strength lies in timing and efficiency, allowing
      the defense line to respond quickly to sudden waves or scattered invasions.
      When speed and control matter more than raw power, Azithromycin becomes the
      quiet force that keeps the battlefield in balance.
  Ciprofloxacin:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 3615056532530566104}
    button: {fileID: 7003118607003265452}
    name: Ciprofloxacin
    description: Ciprofloxacin is a precision enforcer, engineered to hunt down fast-moving
      and hard-to-control bacterial threats. It strikes swiftly at the core of bacterial
      activity, disrupting their ability to spread and regroup across the battlefield.
      While not meant for reckless deployment, its focused power makes it highly
      effective against aggressive waves that rely on speed and momentum. When enemies
      push forward with relentless pressure, Ciprofloxacin answers with calculated
      force, restoring control through decisive and targeted defense.
  Levofloksasin:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 5657185579114909614}
    button: {fileID: 8785229567336180752}
    name: Levofloksasin
    description: Levofloksasin is an advanced guardian refined for absolute control
      on the battlefield. Building upon precision based defenses, it delivers sustained
      pressure that disrupts bacterial movement and prevents coordinated advances.
      More stable and consistent than its predecessors, Levofloxacin excels in prolonged
      encounters where control and reliability determine survival. When waves grow
      relentless and chaos threatens the defense line, its calm and calculated force
      restores order and secures the field.
  Cotrimoxazole:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 2152322085981958719}
    button: {fileID: 3262740782598018356}
    name: Cotrimoxazole
    description: Cotrimoxazole is a coordinated defender that strikes through synergy
      rather than single force. By combining two complementary mechanisms, it blocks
      bacterial survival from multiple directions, leaving enemies with little room
      to adapt or recover. Its strength lies in persistence wearing down waves that
      rely on endurance and gradual advancement. On the battlefield, Cotrimoxazole
      excels at breaking prolonged assaults, proving that cooperation and balance
      can be just as powerful as raw strength in defending the final line.
  Ceftria:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 6431614371343722160}
    button: {fileID: 3314912523506508951}
    name: Ceftriaxone
    description: Ceftria is a precise long-range marksman of the frontline, armed
      with a syringe-fed injector. Built from a third-generation cephalosporin, it
      breaks down the cell walls of fast-growing bacteria before they can regroup.
      It is deadly against the gonorrhea-causing Neisseria and most gram-negative
      invaders, yet it can do nothing against Pseudomonas or MRSA. Strike early with
      Ceftria and the lane stays quiet.
  Clarith:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 8069949984791863064}
    button: {fileID: 6891264739515744661}
    name: Clarithromycin
    description: Clarith is a patient hunter that goes after the foes nobody else
      can reach. As a macrolide antibiotic it halts protein production inside bacteria,
      and it shines against Helicobacter pylori, the spiral invader of the stomach.
      On its own its range of targets is narrow, but fighting beside Amoxicillin
      it becomes part of the strongest combination on the field.
  Colistin:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 8667942654753476277}
    button: {fileID: 3910543588274344946}
    name: Colistin
    description: Colistin is the last resort of the battlefield, a veteran that was
      almost retired before the world needed it again. It barely scratches ordinary
      bacteria, but against the carbapenem-resistant Acinetobacter baumannii nothing
      hits harder. Its power comes at a cost, so call on Colistin only when every
      other defender has failed.
  Doxy:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 2283113394347556885}
    button: {fileID: 2278719084799437269}
    name: Doxycycline
    description: Doxy is a tireless support fighter with a wide but modest reach.
      As a tetracycline antibiotic it shuts down the machinery bacteria use to build
      proteins, which lets it follow enemies even inside cells. Its true specialty
      is Chlamydia trachomatis, a foe that hides where most defenders cannot attack.
  Linezo:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 6205193561760379977}
    button: {fileID: 3217098348875890533}
    name: Linezolid
    description: Linezo is the gram-positive specialist, a cool-headed researcher
      armed with an oxazolidinone shot. Gram-negative bacteria shrug off its attacks
      completely, but MRSA and the vancomycin-resistant Enterococcus fall quickly.
      When vancomycin stops working, Linezo is the one the squad calls.
  Merope:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 3416404993532022808}
    button: {fileID: 8787471030277094018}
    name: Meropenem
    description: Merope is the heavy hitter of the squad, a broad-spectrum carbapenem
      with a punch that reaches almost every gram-negative enemy. ESBL-producing
      Klebsiella, E. coli and Pseudomonas all fall in a few hits. Even so, MRSA,
      VRE and CRAB are immune to it, so Merope needs allies who can cover those weaknesses.
  Penicilin:
    pictureObj: {fileID: 9041397760643062154}
    button: {fileID: 4342217023695867492}
    name: Penicillin V
    description: Penicilin is the old veteran of the roster, the narrowest but sharpest
      fighter on the field. Natural penicillin has been the gold standard against
      Streptococcus pyogenes, the cause of strep throat, for decades. Outside that
      one specialty its reach is tiny, so place Penicilin where it counts.
--- !u!1 &6594089437462572894
