  m_text: Streptococcus pyogenes advances as a curved chain of round cells, each
    one armed with toxins and surface proteins that blind the host's defenses. It
    starts in the throat, where it causes the sharp pain known as strep throat. If
    ignored, it can leave lasting damage to the heart and kidneys long after the
    battle seems won. Fortunately, an old and reliable weapon still brings it down
    every time.
