      m_Calls: []
  m_text: Klebsiella pneumoniae (ESBL) enters the battlefield wrapped in a thick
    protective capsule, shrugging off almost every beta-lactam attack. It lurks in
    hospitals, riding on ventilators and catheters, waiting for weakened patients.
    Once it takes hold, it spreads through the lungs and urinary tract while its
    enzymes dismantle the weapons built to stop it. Only the strongest carbapenem
    can break through, reminding players that resistance can turn ordinary enemies
    into critical threats.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
